{
  "version": 2,
  "$comment": [
    "Per-million-token LIST prices, as data. Adding a newly released model",
    "should be an edit to this file — not a code change.",
    "",
    "These are public API list rates. They are NOT what a subscription plan",
    "charges: Claude Pro/Max and ChatGPT plans meter against usage limits, not",
    "per token. Anything derived from this file is a 'what these tokens would",
    "have cost on the API' figure, and the UI must say so.",
    "",
    "THREE TIERS, CHECKED IN ORDER — `overrides`, then `exact`, then `patterns`:",
    "",
    "  overrides  hand-written, per exact model id, wins over everything. This is",
    "             where a considered disagreement with the feed lives, with a",
    "             `reason`. Never touched by the refresh script.",
    "  exact      per exact model id, GENERATED from the LiteLLM feed by",
    "             scripts/refresh-ai-prices.mjs. Rewritten wholesale on refresh —",
    "             do not hand-edit, your edit will be overwritten.",
    "  patterns   hand-written regexes, ORDER SENSITIVE (first match wins, so",
    "             specific before general). The fallback for ids the feed has",
    "             never heard of: dated snapshots (claude-opus-4-5-20251101),",
    "             aliases, and models released between refreshes. This is why",
    "             patterns still earn their place — but they are now the last",
    "             resort rather than the only mechanism, which is what made the",
    "             original mismatch possible.",
    "the model id the transcript reports.",
    "",
    "THERE IS NO CATCH-ALL, DELIBERATELY. An unrecognised model id resolves to",
    "no price and renders as 'unpriced' rather than a plausible wrong number.",
    "The bug this file was extracted to fix was exactly a silent fallback: the",
    "current-Opus rule failed to match `claude-opus-5`, the id fell through to a",
    "catch-all /opus/ rule holding retired Opus 3 rates, and every Opus 5",
    "session was reported at 3x its real cost for two model generations with no",
    "error. docs/contracts/DERIVATION.md:61 — a derived layer must fail loudly,",
    "never return a plausible-looking lesser result unmarked.",
    "",
    "Where a family's rate has been identical across every generation to date",
    "(sonnet, haiku) the pattern stays family-wide. Where it has actually",
    "changed (opus went $15 -> $5) generations are enumerated, so the next one",
    "is unpriced until someone prices it.",
    "",
    "Fields:",
    "  match           regex source, matched case-insensitively",
    "  label           human name for the tier, shown in provenance tooltips",
    "  effective_from  ISO date these rates took effect (for 'when did this",
    "                  rate apply' questions against historical sessions)",
    "  source          where the numbers came from",
    "  assumed         true when the rate is inherited from a sibling model",
    "                  rather than published for this id. Refreshing from the",
    "                  LiteLLM feed (scripts/refresh-ai-prices.mjs) replaces",
    "                  assumed entries with published ones.",
    "  input           fresh (uncached) input tokens",
    "  output          output tokens",
    "  cacheRead       cache-hit input tokens (Anthropic: 10% of input)",
    "  cacheCreation5m cache write, 5-minute TTL (Anthropic: 1.25x input)",
    "  cacheCreation1h cache write, 1-hour TTL (Anthropic: 2.0x input).",
    "                  Equal to the 5m figure where a provider has no TTL split."
  ],
  "refreshed_at": "2026-09-06",
  "exact_source": "LiteLLM model_prices_and_context_window.json",
